      "Place over moderate heat. As the water comes to a boil, lower the heat to a simmer.",
      "Scum will begin to rise to the surface. As it does so, skim it off with a perforated spoon.",
      "At this point, there are two options:\nAdd the rest of the ingredients and simmer for 2 hours or more, as your taste determines.\nSimmer the stock for 4 to 5 hours or more. One hour before the end of the cooking time, add the rest of the ingredients. This latter method will leave a more pronounced flavour of herbs, spices and vegetables while extracting the most out of the chicken.",
